<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely higher on Tuesday following the rise in Treasury bill rates at the auction, traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said banks expected rates to rise.</p>
<p>&quot;With the battering in the stock market, dollar outflows are expected which would put pressure on the peso,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;It might force the Central Bank to increase rates to defend the peso,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the Philippine Stock Exchange index recorded its biggest single-day drop in two years.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 29		 APRIL 28</p>
<p>    1 W		9 13/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9 13/16		 9 13/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9 15/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 M		10			9 15/16</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/16		10</p>
<p>    6 M		10  5/16		10  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		10  5/8		 10  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		30-Apr		  29-Apr</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (63 2) 841-8937</p>
